-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, "Wrongful restraint and wrongful
-- confinement" (ss 339-348) and "Criminal force and assault" (ss 349-358).
--
-- Covers: ss 339, 340 (definitions), 341, 342, 345, 346, 347, 348 (punishing);
-- ss 349, 350, 351 (definitions), 352, 353, 354(1), 354(2), 354A(1),
-- 354A(2), 355, 356, 357, 358 (punishing). ss 343 and 344 are repealed.
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026 (inputs/PC1871.txt).
--
-- Two facts records: `Restraint Facts` (ss 339-348, and s 357's attempt) and
-- `Criminal Force Facts` (ss 349-358). s 357 is on the criminal force record,
-- because its conduct element is the assault; the attempt to confine is a leaf.
--
-- Cross-module joins owed (notes/body-a-coverage.md):
--   s 356 "in committing or attempting to commit theft" - `commits theft`
--   (s 378) is property's; here it is a leaf. The edge body-a -> property is
--   NOT in PLAN.md's list; the leaf stays a leaf until someone rules on it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, Wrongful restraint and wrongful confinement (ss 339-348)`

§§ `The facts of one restraint`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 339-348 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Restraint Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person restrained or confined, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc How the accused restrained or confined the person, as it is to read after "to wit,"; leave blank to omit
    -- s 339
    `voluntarily obstructs that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused voluntarily (s 26A) obstruct the person? The obstruction may be by physical means or by a threat (s 340 illus (b)).
    `so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the obstruction prevent the person from proceeding in some direction? (s 339)
    `in which that person has a right to proceed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person have a right to proceed in that direction? (s 339)
    `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what the accused obstructed a private way over land or water, which he believed in good faith (s 26B) he had a lawful right to obstruct? If so, it is not an offence (s 339 Exception).
    -- s 340
    `in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person prevented from going beyond certain circumscribing limits - a room, a building, a vehicle, a ring of armed men? (s 340)
    -- s 345
    `knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused keep the person confined knowing that a writ for the person's liberation had been duly issued? (s 345)
    -- s 346
    `in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant, or that its place may not be known or discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the confinement done so as to show an intention that it, or where it was, should not be known to anyone interested in the person, or to any public servant? (s 346)
    -- s 347
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person confined to extort property or a valuable security (s 30) from him or someone interested in him? (s 347)
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person confined to constrain him, or someone interested in him, to do something illegal or to give information that may facilitate an offence? (s 347)
    -- s 348
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person confined to extort a confession, or information that may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct? (s 348)
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person confined to constrain restoration of property, satisfaction of a claim or demand, or information leading to restoration of property? (s 348)

§§ `s 339 - wrongful restraint`

-- 339. Whoever voluntarily obstructs any person, so as to prevent that person
--      from proceeding in any direction in which that person has a right to
--      proceed, is said wrongfully to restrain that person.
--      Exception.-The obstruction of a private way over land or water which a
--      person in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to
--      obstruct, is not an offence within the meaning of this section.
@export Whether the accused is said "wrongfully to restrain" a person within section 339 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused obstructed the person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wrongfully restrains` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `voluntarily obstructs that person`
    AND ", so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction in which that person has a right to proceed,"
        ... f's `so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction`
        ... f's `in which that person has a right to proceed`
    AND "Exception.-The obstruction of a private way ... is not an offence within the meaning of this section."
        ... NOT (f's `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct`)

GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of wrongful restraint not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `voluntarily obstructs that person`) "voluntarily obstructs any person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction`) "so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `in which that person has a right to proceed`) "in which that person has a right to proceed"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct`)) "not the obstruction of a private way which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct (s 339 Exception)"),
        (`missing unless` (`wrongfully restrains` f) "the elements of section 339 taken together"))

§§ `s 340 - wrongful confinement`

-- 340. Whoever wrongfully restrains any person in such a manner as to prevent
--      that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits, is
--      said "wrongfully to confine" that person.
@export Whether the accused is said "wrongfully to confine" a person within section 340 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused restrained the person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wrongfully confines` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `wrongfully restrains` f
    ... f's `in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits`

GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of wrongful confinement not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`elements of wrongful restraint not made out` f),
        (`missing unless` (f's `in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits`) "in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits"),
        (`missing unless` (`wrongfully confines` f) "the elements of section 340 taken together"))

GIVEN f     IS A `Restraint Facts`
      what  IS A STRING
      extra IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the restraint recital` f what extra MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", what, " ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), extra, `the to-wit clause` (f's `the manner`)

§§ `s 341 - punishment for wrongful restraint`

-- 341. Whoever wrongfully restrains any person shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine
--      which may extend to $1,500, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 341
`punishment prescribed by s 341` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "341"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 341 of the Penal Code 1871 (wrongful restraint)
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused obstructed the person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 341` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `wrongfully restrains` f
    ... "any person"

@export Frame a charge under section 341 of the Penal Code 1871 (wrongful restraint), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused obstructed the person, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 341` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "341" "wrongful restraint"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 341`'s words)
        (`offence under s 341` f)
        (`the restraint recital` f "wrongfully restrain" "")
        (`elements of wrongful restraint not made out` f)

§§ `s 342 - punishment for wrongful confinement`

-- 342. Whoever wrongfully confines any person shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or
--      with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 342
`punishment prescribed by s 342` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "342"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 342 of the Penal Code 1871 (wrongful confinement)
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 342` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `wrongfully confines` f
    ... "any person"

@export Frame a charge under section 342 of the Penal Code 1871 (wrongful confinement), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 342` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "342" "wrongful confinement"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 342`'s words)
        (`offence under s 342` f)
        (`the restraint recital` f "wrongfully confine" "")
        (`elements of wrongful confinement not made out` f)

-- s 343. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 344. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

§§ `s 345 - wrongful confinement of person for whose liberation a writ has been issued`

-- 345. Whoever keeps any person in wrongful confinement, knowing that a writ
--      for the liberation of that person has been duly issued, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, in
--      addition to any term of imprisonment to which he may be liable under
--      any other section of this Code.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 345
`punishment prescribed by s 345` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "345"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, in addition to any term of imprisonment to which he may be liable under any other section of this Code"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 345 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, and what he knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 345` f IF
        "Whoever keeps any person in"
    ... `wrongfully confines` f
    ... f's `knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued`

@export Frame a charge under section 345 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 345` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "345" "wrongful confinement of person for whose liberation a writ has been issued"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 345`'s words)
        (`offence under s 345` f)
        (`the restraint recital` f "keep in wrongful confinement" ", knowing that a writ for the liberation of the said person had been duly issued")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of wrongful confinement not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued`) "knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued")))

§§ `s 346 - wrongful confinement in secret`

-- 346. Whoever wrongfully confines any person in such a manner as to indicate
--      an intention that the confinement of that person may not be known to
--      any person interested in the person so confined, or to any public
--      servant, or that the place of such confinement may not be known to or
--      discovered by any such person or public servant as hereinbefore
--      mentioned, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 2 years, in addition to any other punishment to which he may
--      be liable for such wrongful confinement.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 346
`punishment prescribed by s 346` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "346"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, in addition to any other punishment to which he may be liable for such wrongful confinement"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 346 of the Penal Code 1871 (wrongful confinement in secret)
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 346` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `wrongfully confines` f
    ... f's `in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant, or that its place may not be known or discovered`

@export Frame a charge under section 346 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 346` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "346" "wrongful confinement in secret"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 346`'s words)
        (`offence under s 346` f)
        (`the restraint recital` f "wrongfully confine" " in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement of the said person may not be known to any person interested in the said person or to any public servant")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of wrongful confinement not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant, or that its place may not be known or discovered`) "in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement, or its place, may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant")))

§§ `s 347 - wrongful confinement for the purpose of extorting property or constraining to an illegal act`

-- 347. Whoever wrongfully confines any person for the purpose of extorting from
--      the person confined, or from any person interested in the person
--      confined, any property or valuable security, or of constraining the
--      person confined, or any person interested in such person, to do
--      anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the
--      commission of an offence, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 347
`punishment prescribed by s 347` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "347"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 347 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 347` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `wrongfully confines` f
    AND (    f's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security`
         OR  f's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence` )

@export Frame a charge under section 347 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, why, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 347` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "347" "wrongful confinement for the purpose of extorting property or constraining to an illegal act"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 347`'s words)
        (`offence under s 347` f)
        (`the restraint recital` f "wrongfully confine" (`joined with` "," (concat (LIST
            (`included if` (f's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security`) " for the purpose of extorting property or a valuable security"),
            (`included if` (f's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence`) " for the purpose of constraining the person confined to do anything illegal or to give information which may facilitate the commission of an offence")))))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of wrongful confinement not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security` OR f's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence`) "for the purpose of extorting property or a valuable security, or of constraining to an illegal act")))

§§ `s 348 - wrongful confinement for the purpose of extorting confession or of compelling restoration of property`

-- 348. Whoever wrongfully confines any person for the purpose of extorting from
--      the person confined, or from any person interested in the person
--      confined, any confession or any information which may lead to the
--      detection of an offence or misconduct, or for the purpose of
--      constraining the person confined, or any person interested in the person
--      confined, to restore, or to cause the restoration of any property or
--      valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give
--      information which may lead to the restoration of any property or
--      valuable security, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
--      may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 348
`punishment prescribed by s 348` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "348"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 348 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 348` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `wrongfully confines` f
    AND (    f's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`
         OR  f's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` )

@export Frame a charge under section 348 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Restraint Facts` @desc How the accused confined the person, why, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 348` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "348" "wrongful confinement for the purpose of extorting confession or of compelling restoration of property"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 348`'s words)
        (`offence under s 348` f)
        (`the restraint recital` f "wrongfully confine" (`joined with` "," (concat (LIST
            (`included if` (f's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`) " for the purpose of extorting a confession or information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct"),
            (`included if` (f's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security`) " for the purpose of constraining the restoration of property or the satisfaction of a claim or demand")))))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of wrongful confinement not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct` OR f's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security`) "for the purpose of extorting a confession, or of compelling restoration of property")))

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, Criminal force and assault (ss 349-358)`

§§ `The facts of one use of force or assault`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 349-358 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Criminal Force Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person to whom force was used or who was assaulted, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by touching the said Z's breast"
    -- s 349 - force
    `causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause the person to move, change motion, or stop moving? (s 349)
    `causes to any substance such motion as brings that substance into contact with that other's body, or with anything he is wearing or carrying, or so situated that the contact affects his sense of feeling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause some substance to move so as to come into contact with the person's body, with what he wore or carried, or with something so placed that he felt it? (s 349)
    `by his own bodily power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause that motion by his own bodily power? (s 349 proviso (a))
    `by disposing any substance so that the motion takes place without any further act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause it by disposing a substance so that the motion took place without any further act by him or anyone else? (s 349 proviso (b))
    `by inducing any animal to move, to change its motion, or to cease to move` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause it by inducing an animal to move, change its motion or stop? (s 349 proviso (c))
    -- s 350 - criminal force
    `intentionally uses force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused use the force intentionally? (s 350; s 26C)
    `without that person's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the force used without the person's consent? (s 350; s 90 for what is not consent)
    `in order to cause the committing of any offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused use the force in order to cause an offence to be committed? (s 350)
    `intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend, by the force, illegally (s 43) to cause the person injury (s 44), fear or annoyance? (s 350)
    `knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused know it likely that the force would illegally cause the person injury, fear or annoyance? (s 350)
    -- s 351 - assault
    `makes any gesture or any preparation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make a gesture or a preparation? Mere words do not amount to an assault, but words may give a gesture or preparation its meaning (s 351 Explanation).
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that it will cause any person present to apprehend that he is about to use criminal force to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend, or know it likely, that the gesture or preparation would make the person, who was present, apprehend that the accused was about to use criminal force to him? (s 351)
    -- ss 352, 355, 358 - grave and sudden provocation, and the s 352 Explanation
    `on grave and sudden provocation given by that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act on grave and sudden provocation given by the person assaulted? A question of fact (s 352 Explanation).
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provocation NOT sought or voluntarily provoked by the accused as an excuse? (s 352 Explanation)
    `the offender does not know or have reason to believe that the provocation is given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused neither know nor have reason to believe that the provocation was given by something done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant lawfully exercising his powers? (s 352 Explanation)
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provocation NOT given by something done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence? (s 352 Explanation)
    -- s 353
    `that person is a public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a public servant within section 21? (drill-down `public servant within section 21`)
    `in the execution of his duty as such public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant executing his duty at the time? (s 353)
    `with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as such public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend to prevent or deter the public servant from discharging his duty? (s 353)
    `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by such person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done because of something the public servant did or tried to do in the lawful discharge of his duty? (s 353)
    -- s 354
    `intending to outrage the modesty of that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend to outrage the person's modesty? (s 354(1))
    `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused know it likely that he would thereby outrage the person's modesty? (s 354(1))
    `that person is below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person below 14 years of age? (ss 354(2), 354A(2)(b); the helper `below 14 years of age` decides it from the age)
    -- s 354A
    `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence against that person under section 354` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: was what follows done in order to commit, or to facilitate, an outrage of modesty under s 354 against the person? (s 354A(1))
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused voluntarily cause, or attempt to cause, the person's death? (s 354A(1))
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person hurt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... hurt (s 319)? (s 354A(1))
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person wrongful restraint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... wrongful restraint (s 339)? (s 354A(1))
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint? (s 354A(1))
    `in a lift in any building` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed in a lift in a building? (s 354A(2)(a))
    -- s 355
    `intending thereby to dishonour that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend thereby to dishonour the person? (s 355)
    -- s 356
    `in committing or attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the force used in committing or attempting theft (s 378) of property the person was wearing or carrying at the time? Theft is property's to define; joined at integration.
    -- s 357
    `in attempting wrongfully to confine that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the force used in attempting wrongfully to confine the person (s 340)? (s 357)

§§ `s 349 - force`

-- 349. A person is said to use force to another if he causes motion, change of
--      motion, or cessation of motion to that other, or if he causes to any
--      substance such motion, or change of motion, or cessation of motion as
--      brings that substance into contact with any part of that other's body,
--      or with anything which that other is wearing or carrying, or with
--      anything so situated that such contact affects that other's sense of
--      feeling:
--      Provided that the person causing the motion ... causes [it] in one of
--      the following 3 ways: (a) by his own bodily power; (b) by disposing any
--      substance in such a manner that the motion, or change or cessation of
--      motion, takes place without any further act on his part, or on the part
--      of any other person; (c) by inducing any animal to move, to change its
--      motion, or to cease to move.
@export Whether the accused is said to "use force" to another within section 349 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What motion the accused caused, and how
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uses force` f IF
        "A person is said to use force to another if he"
    AND (    f's `causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other`
         OR  f's `causes to any substance such motion as brings that substance into contact with that other's body, or with anything he is wearing or carrying, or so situated that the contact affects his sense of feeling` )
    AND "Provided that [he] causes [it] in one of the following 3 ways:"
    AND (    f's `by his own bodily power`
         OR  f's `by disposing any substance so that the motion takes place without any further act`
         OR  f's `by inducing any animal to move, to change its motion, or to cease to move` )

§§ `s 350 - criminal force`

-- 350. Whoever intentionally uses force to any person, without that person's
--      consent, in order to cause the committing of any offence, or intending
--      by the use of such force illegally to cause, or knowing it to be likely
--      that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury, fear or
--      annoyance to the person to whom the force is used, is said to use
--      criminal force to that other.
@export Whether the accused is said to "use criminal force" to another within section 350 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc The force, and what the accused meant or foresaw by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uses criminal force` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `intentionally uses force`
    AND `uses force` f
    AND "to any person,"
    AND f's `without that person's consent`
    AND (    f's `in order to cause the committing of any offence`
         OR  f's `intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person`
         OR  f's `knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person` )

§§ `s 351 - assault`

-- 351. Whoever makes any gesture or any preparation, intending or knowing it
--      to be likely that such gesture or preparation will cause any person
--      present to apprehend that he who makes that gesture or preparation is
--      about to use criminal force to that person, is said to commit an
--      assault.
--      Explanation.-Mere words do not amount to an assault. But the words
--      which a person uses may give to his gestures or preparations such a
--      meaning as may make those gestures or preparations amount to an assault.
@export Whether the accused is said to "commit an assault" within section 351 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc The gesture or preparation, and what the accused meant or foresaw by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits an assault` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `makes any gesture or any preparation`
    ... f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that it will cause any person present to apprehend that he is about to use criminal force to that person`
    ... "is said to commit an assault"

@export Whether the accused "assaults or uses criminal force to" a person (ss 351 and 350 of the Penal Code 1871), the conduct every punishing section of ss 352-358 begins with
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `assaults or uses criminal force` f IF
        `commits an assault` f
    OR  `uses criminal force` f

-- The s 352 Explanation, which ss 355 and 358 adopt: provocation mitigates only
-- if it was grave and sudden, given by the victim, and none of the three
-- disqualifications applies.
@export Whether the accused acted on grave and sudden provocation that mitigates the offence, within section 352 and its Explanation (adopted by sections 355 and 358) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc The provocation, and how it arose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on grave and sudden provocation given by that person, within the Explanation to section 352` f IF
        f's `on grave and sudden provocation given by that person`
    ... "Grave and sudden provocation will not mitigate ... if"
    ... f's `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for the offence`
    ... f's `the offender does not know or have reason to believe that the provocation is given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`
    ... f's `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the force verb` f MEANS
    IF   `uses criminal force` f
    THEN "use criminal force to"
    ELSE "assault"

GIVEN f     IS A `Criminal Force Facts`
      extra IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the force recital` f extra MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", `the force verb` f, " ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), extra, ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of assault or criminal force not made out` f MEANS
    `missing unless` (`assaults or uses criminal force` f) "assaults (s 351) or uses criminal force (s 350) to any person"

§§ `s 352 - punishment for using criminal force otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation`

-- 352. Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any person otherwise than on
--      grave and sudden provocation given by that person, shall be punished
--      with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine
--      which may extend to $1,500, or with both.
--      Explanation.-Grave and sudden provocation will not mitigate the
--      punishment for an offence under this section, if the provocation is
--      sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for the
--      offence; or if the offender knows or has reason to believe that the
--      provocation is given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a
--      public servant in the lawful exercise of the powers of such public
--      servant; or if the provocation is given by anything done in the lawful
--      exercise of the right of private defence. Whether the provocation was
--      grave and sudden enough to mitigate the offence, is a question of fact.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 352
`punishment prescribed by s 352` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "352"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 352 of the Penal Code 1871 (assault or criminal force otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and whether he was provoked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 352` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `assaults or uses criminal force` f
    ... "to any person otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation given by that person"
    ... NOT (`on grave and sudden provocation given by that person, within the Explanation to section 352` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 352 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 352` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "352" "using criminal force otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 352`'s words)
        (`offence under s 352` f)
        (`the force recital` f "")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of assault or criminal force not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT (`on grave and sudden provocation given by that person, within the Explanation to section 352` f)) "otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation given by that person (on such provocation, the offence is section 358)")))

§§ `s 353 - using criminal force to deter a public servant from discharge of his duty`

-- 353. Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any person being a public
--      servant in the execution of his duty as such public servant, or with
--      intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as
--      such public servant, or in consequence of anything done or attempted to
--      be done by such person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such
--      public servant, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 4 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 353
`punishment prescribed by s 353` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "353"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 48
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 353 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, to whom, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 353` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `assaults or uses criminal force` f
    AND "to any person being a"
    AND f's `that person is a public servant`
    AND (    f's `in the execution of his duty as such public servant`
         OR  f's `with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as such public servant`
         OR  f's `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by such person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant` )

@export Frame a charge under section 353 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 353` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "353" "using criminal force to deter a public servant from discharge of his duty"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 353`'s words)
        (`offence under s 353` f)
        (`the force recital` f (CONCAT ", a public servant, ", `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST
            (`included if` (f's `in the execution of his duty as such public servant`) "in the execution of his duty as such public servant"),
            (`included if` (f's `with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as such public servant`) "with intent to deter the said public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant"),
            (`included if` (f's `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by such person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`) "in consequence of anything done by the said public servant in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant")))))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of assault or criminal force not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `that person is a public servant`) "to any person being a public servant (s 21)"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `in the execution of his duty as such public servant` OR f's `with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as such public servant` OR f's `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by such person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`) "in the execution of his duty, or with intent to deter him from it, or in consequence of anything done in the lawful discharge of it")))

§§ `s 354 - assault or use of criminal force to a person with intent to outrage modesty`

-- 354.-(1) Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any person, intending to
--      outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the
--      modesty of that person, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any
--      combination of such punishments.
--   (2) Whoever commits an offence under subsection (1) against any person
--      below 14 years of age shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any
--      combination of such punishments.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 354(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 354(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "354(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 354(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 354(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "354(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused assaulted or used criminal force "intending to outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty" of the person (s 354(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what he meant or foresaw by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `outrages the modesty of that person` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `assaults or uses criminal force` f
    AND "to any person,"
        ... (    f's `intending to outrage the modesty of that person`
             OR  f's `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 354(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (outrage of modesty)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what he meant or foresaw by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 354(1)` f IF
        `outrages the modesty of that person` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 354(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (outrage of modesty of a person below 14 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, to whom, and what he meant or foresaw by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 354(2)` f IF
        "Whoever commits an offence under subsection (1)"
    ... `outrages the modesty of that person` f
    ... "against any person"
    ... f's `that person is below 14 years of age`

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the modesty clause` f MEANS
    CONCAT ", ", `joined with` " and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `intending to outrage the modesty of that person`) "intending to outrage the modesty of the said person"),
        (`included if` (f's `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person`) "knowing it to be likely that you would thereby outrage the modesty of the said person")))

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of outrage of modesty not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`elements of assault or criminal force not made out` f),
        (`missing unless` (f's `intending to outrage the modesty of that person` OR f's `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person`) "intending to outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person"))

@export Frame a charge under section 354(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (outrage of modesty), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 354(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "354(1)" "assault or use of criminal force to a person with intent to outrage modesty"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 354(1)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 354(1)` f)
        (`the force recital` f (`the modesty clause` f))
        (`elements of outrage of modesty not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 354(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (outrage of modesty of a person below 14 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 354(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "354(2)" "assault or use of criminal force to a person below 14 years of age with intent to outrage modesty"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 354(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 354(2)` f)
        (`the force recital` f (CONCAT ", a person below 14 years of age", `the modesty clause` f))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of outrage of modesty not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `that person is below 14 years of age`) "against any person below 14 years of age")))

§§ `s 354A - outraging modesty in certain circumstances`

-- 354A.-(1) Whoever, in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an
--      offence against any person under section 354, voluntarily causes or
--      attempts to cause to that person death, or hurt, or wrongful restraint,
--      or fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint,
--      shall be punished with imprisonment for a term of not less than 2 years
--      and not more than 10 years and with caning.
--   (2) Whoever commits an offence under subsection (1) - (a) in a lift in any
--      building; or (b) against any person below 14 years of age, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not
--      more than 10 years and with caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 354A(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 354A(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "354A(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term of not less than 2 years and not more than 10 years and with caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall be punished with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 354A(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 354A(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "354A(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not more than 10 years and with caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall be punished with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 354A(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (outraging modesty in certain circumstances)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and to what end
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 354A(1)` f IF
        "Whoever,"
    AND f's `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence against that person under section 354`
    AND "voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person"
    AND (    f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death`
         OR  f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person hurt`
         OR  f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person wrongful restraint`
         OR  f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 354A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (outraging modesty in a lift, or against a person below 14 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, where, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 354A(2)` f IF
        "Whoever commits an offence under subsection (1)"
    AND `offence under s 354A(1)` f
    AND (    f's `in a lift in any building`
         OR  f's `that person is below 14 years of age` )

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the s 354A recital` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did, in order to commit an offence under section 354 against ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", voluntarily cause or attempt to cause to the said person ",
        `joined with` " or " (concat (LIST
            (`included if` (f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death`) "death"),
            (`included if` (f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person hurt`) "hurt"),
            (`included if` (f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person wrongful restraint`) "wrongful restraint"),
            (`included if` (f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint`) "fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint"))),
        ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of section 354A(1) not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence against that person under section 354`) "in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence against that person under section 354"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death` OR f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person hurt` OR f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person wrongful restraint` OR f's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint`) "voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death, hurt, wrongful restraint, or fear of instant death, hurt or wrongful restraint"))

@export Frame a charge under section 354A(1) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 354A(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "354A(1)" "outraging modesty in certain circumstances"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 354A(1)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 354A(1)` f)
        (`the s 354A recital` f)
        (`elements of section 354A(1) not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 354A(2) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 354A(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "354A(2)" "outraging modesty in certain circumstances"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 354A(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 354A(2)` f)
        (CONCAT (`the s 354A recital` f), `joined with` "" (concat (LIST
            (`included if` (f's `in a lift in any building`) ", the offence being committed in a lift in a building"),
            (`included if` (f's `that person is below 14 years of age`) ", the said person being below 14 years of age"))))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of section 354A(1) not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `in a lift in any building` OR f's `that person is below 14 years of age`) "in a lift in any building, or against any person below 14 years of age")))

§§ `s 355 - assault or criminal force with intent to dishonour otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation`

-- 355. Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any person, intending thereby
--      to dishonour that person, otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation
--      given by that person, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
--      Explanation.-This section is subject to the same explanation as
--      section 352.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 355
`punishment prescribed by s 355` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "355"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 355 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant by it, and whether he was provoked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 355` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `assaults or uses criminal force` f
    ... f's `intending thereby to dishonour that person`
    ... "otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation given by that person"
    ... NOT (`on grave and sudden provocation given by that person, within the Explanation to section 352` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 355 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 355` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "355" "assault or criminal force with intent to dishonour otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 355`'s words)
        (`offence under s 355` f)
        (`the force recital` f ", intending thereby to dishonour the said person")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of assault or criminal force not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending thereby to dishonour that person`) "intending thereby to dishonour that person"),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT (`on grave and sudden provocation given by that person, within the Explanation to section 352` f)) "otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation given by that person")))

§§ `s 356 - assault or criminal force in committing or attempting to commit theft of property carried by a person`

-- 356. Whoever assaults or uses criminal force on any person, in committing or
--      attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then
--      wearing or carrying, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term of
--      not less than one year and not more than 7 years, and shall also be
--      liable to caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 356
`punishment prescribed by s 356` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "356"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term of not less than one year and not more than 7 years, and shall also be liable to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 356 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and in the course of what
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 356` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `assaults or uses criminal force` f
    ... f's `in committing or attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying`

@export Frame a charge under section 356 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Force Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 356` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "356" "assault or criminal force in committing or attempting to commit theft of property carried by a person"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 356`'s words)
        (`offence under s 356` f)
        (`the force recital` f ", in committing or attempting to commit theft of property which the said person was then wearing or carrying")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of assault or criminal force not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `in committing or attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying`) "in committing or attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying")))

§§ `s 357 - assault or criminal force in attempting wrongfully to confine a person`

